UPDATE companies SET description='Kobelco Aluminum Automotive Products (KAAP) was established in 2005 in Bowling Green, Kentucky, as the U.S. operating arm of the Kobe Steel Group, known globally under the KOBELCO brand. The Japanese parent company, founded in 1937, entered the Kentucky community nearly two decades ago and has since invested in six facility expansions to build out forging capacity.

The plant specializes in aluminum forgings for automotive suspension components and cast rods for compressor applications, serving global automakers and tier-one suppliers. KAAP combines advanced engineering with high-volume forging and casting processes, though specific headcount, floor space, or annual part numbers are not publicly disclosed.

Its customer base centers on the automotive industry, with documented quality awards from Honda (Excellence in Quality), Nissan (Quality and Zero Defect), and Subaru (Excellent Performance). The company also supplies cast rods for compressor manufacturers, extending its reach beyond vehicle chassis into thermal-management systems.

KAAP cites its guiding principle, "Sei shin sei i" — put your heart and soul into your work — as the cultural foundation for its safety and environmental programs. The company emphasizes that its lightweight aluminum components reduce vehicle mass, lower fuel consumption, and cut carbon emissions, aligning product performance with sustainability goals.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aluminum forging", "Cast rod production for compressors", "Advanced engineering", "Global distribution"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Compressor"], "materials": ["Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Six facility expansions since 2005 adding forging equipment and expertise", "Aluminum forgings for automotive suspensions and cast rods for compressors", "Quality awards from Honda, Nissan, and Subaru", "Part of the Kobe Steel Group (KOBELCO) with global materials and machinery reputation", "Mission-driven culture: \"Sei shin sei i\" (Put your heart and soul into your work)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2005 in Bowling Green, Kentucky -> /about", "Part of Kobe Steel Group (KOBELCO) -> /about", "Produces aluminum forgings for automotive suspensions and cast rods for compressors -> /", "Six facility expansions since 2005 -> /", "Quality awards from Honda, Nissan, Subaru -> /about", "Mission: Sei shin sei i (Put your heart and soul into your work) -> /about", "Emission reduction focus: lightweight aluminum reduces fuel consumption and carbon output -> /about", "Global leader in forged aluminum technology -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kobelco Aluminum Automotive Products excels in producing and distributing aluminum forgings for automotive suspensions and cast rods for compressors globally.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kobelco-aluminum-automotive-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kokusai, Inc. was founded in 1969 by Shigeru Matsumoto and is headquartered in Indianapolis, Indiana, with its global head office in Tokyo, Japan. The company employs over 300 people worldwide and reports annual sales of approximately $120 million.

The company designs and builds custom production and laboratory testing equipment for the automotive and tire industries. Its product line includes dynamic tire balancing machines, tire and tire/wheel uniformity testers, bead seating systems, wheel gauge uniformity and balancing equipment, precision balancers, shaft straightening machines, compression testers, coil winding testers, vibration and impact testers, servo motor controlled specialized testers, and torsion and tensile testers.

Kokusai serves automotive Tier 1 and Tier 2 suppliers as well as tire manufacturers, providing equipment that meets exacting demands for tire uniformity and quality. The company''s machines are used for testing tire and wheel assemblies, force components, and small components across the automotive supply chain.

