UPDATE companies SET description='LGC Maine Standards operates from Cumberland Foreside, Maine. The business traces its lineage to Maine Standards Company, LLC, which was acquired by LGC in November 2015 and rebranded as LGC Maine Standards. LGC itself dates back to 1842 as the UK Government Chemist and was privatized in 1996; it is now owned by funds affiliated with KKR.

The company manufactures linearity and calibration verification products, most notably the VALIDATE® line of liquid, ready‑to‑use, multi‑level sets configured for widely used clinical instruments. Production takes place in a modern laboratory using streamlined processes, and the firm emphasizes a global logistics network that ships on the customer’s schedule. LGC’s broader operations employ over 2,000 people across 22 countries, though headcount for the Maine site is not disclosed.

Primary customers are clinical laboratories in the diagnostics sector, but LGC’s measurement products and services also serve pharmaceuticals, agricultural biotechnology, food, environment, government, and academia.

Maine Standards states that its 100 % satisfaction guarantee reflects more than 100 years of combined experience in linearity and calibration verification. The company’s stated purpose is to improve the quality of human diagnostics, and it adheres to the AdvaMed Code of Ethics for interactions with healthcare professionals.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO/IEC 17025','GMP','GLP','ISO Guide 34','ISO/IEC 17043','ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Linearity verification product manufacturing", "Calibration verification product manufacturing", "Liquid ready-to-use multi-level set production", "VALIDATE\u00ae product line configuration", "Reference material production", "Proficiency testing services", "Genomics reagent manufacturing", "Instrumentation development", "Expert sample analysis and interpretation", "Technical support", "Global logistics and scheduled shipping"], "industries": ["Diagnostics", "Pharmaceuticals", "Agricultural Biotechnology", "Food", "Environment", "Government", "Academia", "Clinical laboratories"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Liquid, ready\u2011to\u2011use, multi\u2011level calibration sets", "Shipping on the customer\u2019s schedule", "Expert technical support", "100\u202f% customer satisfaction guarantee"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Cumberland Foreside, Maine -> db", "Acquired by LGC in November 2015 -> /about", "LGC history dates to 1842, privatized 1996, owned by KKR-affiliated funds -> /about", "Manufactures linearity and calibration verification products, VALIDATE\u00ae line -> /, /about", "Liquid, ready-to-use, multi-level sets -> /", "Shipping on customer schedule, expert technical support, global logistics, 100% satisfaction guarantee -> /", "Serves diagnostics, pharmaceuticals, agricultural biotechnology, food, environment, government, academia -> /about", "Certifications: ISO/IEC 17025, GMP, GLP, ISO Guide 34, ISO/IEC 17043, ISO 13485:2016 -> /about", "Complies with AdvaMed Code of Ethics -> /about", "LGC employs over 2,000 people in 22 countries -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Maine Standards is a market leader for linearity and calibration verification products. Our modern laboratory and streamlined processes allow us to consistently manufacture products that are of the highest quality, are easy-to-use and are incredibly efficient.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lgc-clinical-diagnostics-maine-standards' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LGND Energy was founded in 2019 in Albuquerque, New Mexico, by brothers Elmer and Octavio Reyna. After years sales teams at larger solar firms, the pair wanted to bring a family-oriented culture to both their representatives and customers, so they launched their own solar sales dealership with a mission to pass savings directly to homeowners.

The company designs, sells, and installs residential and commercial photovoltaic systems across Albuquerque and Bernalillo County. Its services include roof consultations to verify structural readiness, full permitting and HOA coordination, and battery-backup installation using Tesla Powerwall 3 and Enphase units. Field crews, often including father-and-son teams, also fit critter guards and clean arrays.

LGND serves homeowners, small and large businesses, and multi-family properties throughout central New Mexico.

