UPDATE companies SET description='Laguna Fabrics was founded in 1986 in Los Angeles, California, by Monet Goode and has been operated by the Roshan family across multiple generations. The family-owned company began as a circular knit mill serving the contemporary fashion market.

The company produces sustainable circular knit fabrics using in-house knitting machines ranging from low to fine gauge, with a capacity of 1.5 million pounds per month. Its 40-person team handles fabric development, technical analysis, new construction engineering, and sample yardage production. Special finishes include brushing, sueding, and fabric laundering, supported by a multi-layer quality control protocol and an on-site knitting technician.

Laguna serves contemporary fashion brands, young designers, and start-ups seeking sustainable domestic textiles. Longtime clients rely on the mill''s quick turnaround and in-stock natural fiber yarns such as GOTS-certified organic cotton, TENCEL™ lyocell and modal, recycled cotton, and hemp.

Since 2000, Laguna has prioritized lower-impact materials, and in 2019 became the only circular knit mill in the United States with GOTS certification. The company''s stated goal is to reach 90% sustainable material output by 2025, guided by core values of provenance, process transparency, and product authenticity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Circular knitting (low to fine gauge)", "Fabric development", "Technical fabric analysis", "New construction engineering", "Sample yardage production", "Lab dip catalog/color reference", "Showroom appointments", "Brushing and sueding finishes", "Fabric laundering", "Multi-layer quality control (QC/QA)", "In-stock natural fiber yarn sourcing", "On-site knitting technician support"], "industries": ["Contemporary fashion", "Apparel brands", "Sustainable textiles", "Start-up fashion designers", "Domestic textile manufacturing"], "materials": ["GOTS Organic Cotton", "TENCEL\u2122 Lyocell", "TENCEL\u2122 Modal", "Recycled Cotton", "Hemp", "Certified sustainable fibers"], "equipment": ["Circular knitting machines (low to fine gauge)", "Brushing and sueding equipment", "Fabric laundering equipment"], "volume": "1.5 million pounds per month knitting capacity", "lead_time": "Quick turnaround (domestic manufacturing in LA)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only circular knit mill in the U.S. with GOTS certification (since 2019)", "In-house circular knitting capacity of 1.5 million pounds per month", "Domestic manufacturing in Los Angeles enabling quick turnaround", "Focus on certified sustainable fibers: GOTS organic cotton, TENCEL\u2122, recycled cotton, hemp", "Family-owned since 1986 with multi-generational textile expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 in Los Angeles, California -> /about", "Family-owned, Roshan family multi-generational -> /about", "Founder Monet Goode -> /about", "40 employees -> db, /about", "In-house circular knitting machines low to fine gauge -> /about", "1.5 million pounds per month knitting capacity -> /about", "Special finishes: brushing, sueding, fabric laundering -> /about", "Multi-layer quality control protocol -> /about", "On-site knitting technician -> /about", "Services: fabric development, technical analysis, new construction engineering, sample yardage, lab dip catalog, showroom -> /about", "Materials: GOTS Organic Cotton, TENCEL Lyocell, TENCEL Modal, Recycled Cotton, Hemp -> /about, /", "GOTS certified 2019, only circular knit mill in USA with GOTS -> /about", "Goal 90% sustainable material output by 2025 -> /about", "Core values: provenance, process, transparency, product authenticity -> /, /about", "Serves contemporary fashion brands, young designers, start-ups -> /about, /", "Quick turnaround due to domestic manufacturing -> /, /about", "10+ million yards produced with Organic Cotton & TENCEL -> /about", "70%+ fabric produced with certified sustainable fibers -> /about", "71% female / 29% male in management positions -> /about", "Timeline milestones (2000 TENCEL, 2006 organic cotton, 2007 Enviro Fabrics, 2017 GRS recycled cotton, 2018 Textile Exchange, 2019 GOTS, 2021 C4, 2023 merge) -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We proudly manufacture all fabrics in our knitting mill in Los Angeles, California", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "40", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='laguna-fabrics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company distributes a vast inventory of electrical control components, solenoid valves, drives, switches, process motor controls, PLCs, HMIs, and explosion-proof parts from over 100 approved manufacturers. Beyond distribution, Lakeland provides engineering services, rents electrical test and power monitoring equipment, manages customer inventory to prevent supply-chain disruptions, and fabricates custom electrical enclosures through its Delta Fabricating division.

Lakeland serves industrial and commercial customers who rely on electrical controls, instrumentation, and component protection. Its clients include operations that need reliable component supply, custom enclosure solutions, and rental equipment for quality monitoring and power testing.

