UPDATE companies SET description='Lexco Cable Manufacturing operates from Norridge, Illinois, where it has produced custom wire rope, cable, and bungee cord assemblies since 1974. The family-owned company began as a specialist in load-rated termination solutions for OEMs and industrial buyers, growing into a full-service fabricator of wire rope fittings, push-pull controls, architectural cable railings, and related hardware.

The shop handles custom cut-to-length wire rope, crimping, swaging, and assembly of fittings such as end terminals, turnbuckles, and lanyards. Capabilities span prototype through high-volume runs with flexible order quantities and low minimums.

Customers include military prime contractors, OEMs in fitness and agriculture, MRO distributors, general contractors, and aftermarket sellers. The company''s product line addresses applications from aircraft cable assemblies meeting MIL-DTL-83420 to bungee cords for tethering and sign hanging, with a configurator that lets buyers specify diameter, construction, coating, and end fittings.

